      "note": "Yamaha DM7 Series Reference Manual, general specifications, opened 2026-11-12: 793 x 324 x 564 mm (W x H x D) including rubber feet, 23.5 kg (the DM7 Compact is a different size). Rear panel (from the manual and the Yamaha download): INPUT 1-32 on XLR (female, +48 V per input), OMNI OUT 1-16 (XLR male), AES/EBU IN 1/2 and 3/4 and OUT 1/2 and 3/4 (XLR), word clock in and out (BNC), GPI (D-sub 15, not modelled), PY card slot, Dante PRIMARY and SECONDARY (etherCON, 144 channels), USB TO HOST (USB-C, 18 in and out), network RJ45, two AC IN inlets (V-lock, type letter not named: iec-c14 assumed for the one modelled, plan assumedConnectors power-in), one power switch on the rear; front/top: stereo phones, USB storage ports (number not stated). Modelled: 8 of 32 inputs, 8 of 16 outputs, 2 of 2 AES in and 2 of 2 AES out. TC IN (timecode) is not modelled. Generic artwork only (content/generic-panels/<id>.json, drawn by npm run asset:panel): connectors, faders, knobs and screens drawn without lettering, no photo, no logo. Every port and control position is a guess (confidence guess) and the side profile is an estimate drawn from the three outer sizes (no drawing opened). Connector genders not stated by the source follow the convention input = female, output = male."
